      'what is the difference between a waterspout and a landspout non mesocyclonic non supercell fair weather bottom up versus tornadic waterspout',
      'a LANDSPOUT is a weak generally short lived TORNADO over land that is NON MESOCYCLONIC it does NOT descend from a rotating supercell updraft instead it forms from the BOTTOM UP low level spin along a boundary or convergence line gets stretched vertically by a growing ordinary cumulus congestus or young thunderstorm updraft usually EF0 to EF1 narrow rope like and lasts only minutes',
