      'a MICROBURST is a small intense downdraft from a thunderstorm under 4 km wide that hits the ground and spreads out as a burst of damaging straight line winds over 100 mph in extreme cases a serious aviation hazard on approach and takeoff the WET versus DRY label is about WHAT DRIVES the downdraft and whether rain reaches the ground not about stages',
