      'a DRY LINE also called a dew point front is a MOISTURE boundary with little or no temperature change across it it separates warm MOIST air usually from the Gulf of Mexico to its east from hot DRY air from the desert Southwest or Mexican plateau to its west when it passes the DEW POINT crashes maybe 15 to 30 F in an hour the air feels suddenly drier humidity plummets but the temperature may even rise',
      'the dry line is a classic severe weather and tornado trigger on the US Southern Plains Texas Oklahoma Kansas it bulges eastward during the afternoon and retreats west overnight storms fire along it where the moist air is lifted over the advancing dry air',
